{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For YHWH your Elohim hardened his spirit and made his heart obstinate.</b> This expression is not used of the Holy One, blessed be He, except regarding absolute wicked ones such as Pharaoh and Sihon, who had already rendered themselves liable, by virtue of their wickedness, to have the paths of repentance withheld from them. And since they come against HaShem, may He be exalted, and rebel against Him, the Holy One, blessed be He, strengthens their heart so that even if they wish to retract, they are unable to do so. And we do not find in the Torah 'and YHWH strengthened Pharaoh's heart' — rather, Scripture mentioned it four times: 'and Pharaoh's heart was hardened,' 'and he made his heart heavy,' 'and his heart was heavy,' and 'Pharaoh's heart was heavy.' And similarly we find regarding Elijah, who said (I Kings 18:37): ״ואתה הסבות את לבם אחורנית״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Reader's note: the four citation phrases appear to reference Exodus passages on Pharaoh's heart (Exodus 7–9)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:57.323387138Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}